{
  "_comment": "LoopStar's own amps, cabinets and pedal voicings (asked 2026-11-17: 'warm guitar tube emulators'). The iPhone's engine (LoopStar/DSP/LoopStarDSP.c) is generic; THIS file says what each amp is. An amp: tightHz = input high-pass; preMid = a mid push before the gain (db 0 = none); gainDB = what the Gain knob spans; stages = two triode stages (gain into tanh(u + bias) - tanh(bias): bias makes the even harmonics; lowPassHz = the stage's Miller roll-off); couplingHz = the coupling caps' high-pass; toneStack = a key of toneStacks (the passive treble/bass/mid network: farads and ohms); toneMakeupDB = its loss made up; power = the power stage (driveDB into it, sag 0-1 = how much a loud note squeezes the supply, releaseMs, bias); presenceDB (high shelf 3.5 kHz) and depthDB (100 Hz) after it; cab = a cabinet id (its filters run after the amp; 'none' = into a real amp); outputDB = the model's trim so every amp sits at about the same loudness at its default knobs (set by the calibration in the DSP test harness, not by ear alone); knobs = the defaults a preset without its own takes. Cabinet filters: type lowpass|highpass|peak|lowshelf|highshelf, hz, q, db (peak/shelf). pedals.wah = the wah's sweep (heel lowHz to toe highHz) and q. Names are our own: never an amp maker's or a model's trademark. Edit here; zero rebuild (the app also ships a frozen copy as its offline floor). pedals.comp.styles (2026-11-18): LoopStar's own compressor, one knob (the preset's comp.amount / the board's Squeeze) spanning thresholdMinDB..thresholdMaxDB (dB of the peak detector) and ratioMin..ratioMax; kneeDB soft knee; attackMs; releaseFastMs after a short loud moment, releaseSlowMs after a stretch of compression (an optical cell's recovery); makeup is automatic: the reduction a signal at makeupRefDB (dBFS) would get is given back, so a voice at a typical level comes out as loud as it went in at any amount; warmth is a tanh drive after it (0 = none, 1.2 = a touch of second harmonic with bias 0.08); sidechainHz high-passes the detector so the low end doesn't pump it. A preset picks one with comp: {style, amount}; no style = Apple's compressor, as before.",
